---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { seoMetadata } from "../lib/constants";

const pageMetadata = seoMetadata["/mandalafy/"];

const experience = [
  {
    title: "Easy to begin",
    description:
      "The symmetry provides an immediate structure, so you can start making choices without needing a complete plan.",
  },
  {
    title: "Absorbing to use",
    description:
      "Color, repetition, rhythm, and immediate visual feedback can draw your attention into the developing design.",
  },
  {
    title: "Open to discovery",
    description:
      "Each choice changes what comes next. Unexpected relationships emerge as the pattern becomes more complex.",
  },
  {
    title: "Distinctly yours",
    description:
      "The tool supplies the structure, but you choose every color, gesture, placement, and direction.",
  },
];

const steps = [
  {
    number: "01",
    title: "Choose",
    description:
      "Select colors, shapes, line styles, symmetry, and other elements that will influence the design.",
  },
  {
    number: "02",
    title: "Create",
    description:
      "Draw and experiment while each gesture is repeated around the center of the mandala.",
  },
  {
    number: "03",
    title: "Respond",
    description:
      "Notice what is emerging, revise your choices, and continue developing the composition.",
  },
  {
    number: "04",
    title: "Keep or share",
    description:
      "Save the finished image or, if you choose, place your design on a product.",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={pageMetadata.title}
  description={pageMetadata.description}
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section
    class="relative overflow-hidden border-b border-gray-200 bg-white dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900"
  >
    <div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0" aria-hidden="true">
      <div
        class="absolute -right-24 top-4 h-96 w-96 rounded-full bg-fuchsia-100/70 blur-3xl dark:bg-fuchsia-900/20"
      >
      </div>

      <div
        class="absolute -left-24 bottom-0 h-80 w-80 rounded-full bg-amber-100/60 blur-3xl dark:bg-amber-900/20"
      >
      </div>
    </div>

    <div
      class="relative mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-12 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-28 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_0.86fr] lg:gap-20 lg:px-8 lg:py-32"
    >
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400"
        >
          Interactive creativity
        </p>

        <h1
          class="mt-6 text-5xl font-bold leading-[1.04] tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl"
        >
          Mandalafy
        </h1>

        <p
          class="mt-7 max-w-2xl text-2xl leading-9 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"
        >
          Create a mandala one choice at a time.
        </p>

        <div
          class="mt-6 max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300"
        >
          <p>
            Mandalafy is a free interactive design tool that turns simple
            gestures into symmetrical patterns.
          </p>

          <p>
            You choose the colors, shapes, placement, rhythm, and direction.
            The structure helps you begin, but the finished design emerges
            through your decisions.
          </p>

          <p>
            Create for the experience itself, save what you make, or place the
            finished design on a product if you choose.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
          <a
            href="https://mandalafy.com/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-6 py-3 font-medium text-white transition-colors hover:bg-blue-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-2 dark:focus:ring-offset-gray-900"
          >
            Create a mandala
            <span class="ml-2" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>

          <a
            href="#how-it-works"
            class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-6 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-100 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-2 dark:border-gray-700 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-gray-800 dark:focus:ring-offset-gray-900"
          >
            See how it works
            <span class="ml-2" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure>
        <div
          class="overflow-hidden rounded-[2rem] border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-4 shadow-xl shadow-gray-200/60 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-950 dark:shadow-black/20 sm:p-6"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/mandala2.webp"
            alt="A colorful geometric mandala created with Mandalafy"
            class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl object-cover"
            width="900"
            height="900"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Introduction -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div
      class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-8 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[0.42fr_1fr] lg:px-8 lg:py-28"
    >
      <div>
        <p
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400"
        >
          Structure and freedom
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h2
          class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white sm:text-4xl"
        >
          A simple framework can open a surprising amount of possibility.
        </h2>

        <div
          class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300"
        >
          <p>
            A blank canvas can feel liberating, but it can also make it hard to
            know where to begin. Mandalafy offers a starting structure:
            rotational symmetry around a shared center.
          </p>

          <p>
            Each mark is repeated across the design. A small movement can
            become a flower, a wheel, a field of overlapping shapes, or
            something that does not resemble anything you expected.
          </p>

          <p>
            The pattern gives your choices coherence without deciding what
            those choices should be.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it works -->
  <section
    id="how-it-works"
    class="scroll-mt-24 border-y border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-950"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400"
        >
          How it works
        </p>

        <h2
          class="mt-5 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white sm:text-5xl"
        >
          Make a choice. See what happens. Continue from there.
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          There is no single correct sequence and no required finished result.
          The process develops through experimentation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="mt-14 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        {
          steps.map((step) => (
            <li
              class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-7 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900 sm:p-8"
            >
              <span
                class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                {step.number}
              </span>

              <h3
                class="mt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
              >
                {step.title}
              </h3>

              <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
                {step.description}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Creative experience -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-28">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <p
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400"
        >
          The creative experience
        </p>

        <h2
          class="mt-5 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white sm:text-5xl"
        >
          The experience of making matters as much as the finished image.
        </h2>

        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Mandalafy is designed to make creativity approachable, active, and
          rewarding throughout the process.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          experience.map((item, index) => (
            <article
              class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-7 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-950 sm:p-8"
            >
              <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
                <span class="pt-1 font-mono text-xs text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500">
                  {String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}
                </span>

                <div>
                  <h3
                    class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white"
                  >
                    {item.title}
                  </h3>

                  <p
                    class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300"
                  >
                    {item.description}
                  </p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Making with a tool -->
  <section
    class="border-y border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-950"
  >
    <div
      class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-12 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[0.88fr_1.12fr] lg:gap-20 lg:px-8 lg:py-28"
    >
      <figure>
        <div
          class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-gray-200 bg-white p-4 shadow-sm dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900 sm:p-6"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/mandala-woven-sunlight-660.webp"
            alt="A detailed mandala with layered geometric patterns and warm colors"
            class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl object-cover"
            width="660"
            height="660"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <div>
        <p
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400"
        >
          Making with a tool
        </p>

        <h2
          class="mt-5 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white sm:text-5xl"
        >
          The software extends each gesture without taking over the work.
        </h2>

        <div
          class="mt-7 space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300"
        >
          <p>
            Mandalafy does not ask you to describe an image and wait for a
            finished result. You remain involved throughout the process.
          </p>

          <p>
            Every line changes the composition. Each choice creates new
            relationships, and you respond to what is already present much as
            you might respond to paint, clay, sound, or another creative
            medium.
          </p>

          <p>
            The tool handles repetition and symmetry. You provide the
            direction, judgment, curiosity, and willingness to experiment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Beyond the screen -->
  <section class="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
    <div
      class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-center gap-12 px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_0.88fr] lg:gap-20 lg:px-8 lg:py-28"
    >
      <div>
        <p
          class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400"
        >
          Beyond the screen
        </p>

        <h2
          class="mt-5 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white sm:text-5xl"
        >
          The design can remain an image—or become part of everyday life.
        </h2>

        <div
          class="mt-7 space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300"
        >
          <p>
            Creating the mandala can be the entire experience. The tool is free
            to use, and there is no need to buy anything.
          </p>

          <p>
            You can save the finished design as a digital image. When you want
            something tangible, you can also place it on a print, notebook,
            shirt, or another available product.
          </p>

          <p>
            The product is optional. The design—and the experience of creating
            it—comes first.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure>
        <div
          class="rounded-3xl border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-950 sm:p-8"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/SubtleCircles.webp"
            alt="An abstract arrangement of circular forms suggesting pattern and connection"
            class="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg"
            width="1200"
            height="675"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Ongoing project -->
  <section
    class="border-t border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-950"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 lg:py-28">
      <div
        class="rounded-3xl border border-gray-200 bg-white px-6 py-14 dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-900 sm:px-10 lg:px-14 lg:py-20"
      >
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <p
            class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400"
          >
            An ongoing creative project
          </p>

          <h2
            class="mt-5 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 dark:text-white sm:text-5xl"
          >
            Mandalafy continues to change through making and use.
          </h2>

          <div
            class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300"
          >
            <p>
              I continue to create with Mandalafy, refine the software, and
              explore what the tool can become.
            </p>

            <p>
              The best way to understand the project is not simply to read
              about it, but to make something.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
            <a
              href="https://mandalafy.com/"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
              class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-6 py-3 font-medium text-white transition-colors hover:bg-blue-700 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-2 dark:focus:ring-offset-gray-900"
            >
              Create with Mandalafy
              <span class="ml-2" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>

            <a
              href="/projects/"
              class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-gray-300 px-6 py-3 font-medium text-gray-900 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-100 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 focus:ring-offset-2 dark:border-gray-700 dark:text-white dark:hover:bg-gray-800 dark:focus:ring-offset-gray-900"
            >
              Return to projects
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>